WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.858 --> 00:00:01.392
One grinder said it was nice to

00:00:01.659 --> 00:00:03.194
be back on the court in a real

00:00:03.828 --> 00:00:05.863
game and love from the fans was

00:00:06.330 --> 00:00:06.864
amazing.

00:00:06.864 --> 00:00:08.332
&gt;&gt; The CIA is trying to

00:00:08.332 --> 00:00:10.968
convince Russian spies to spill

00:00:11.235 --> 00:00:11.735
their secrets.

00:00:11.836 --> 00:00:12.970
Launching a new social media

00:00:13.237 --> 00:00:14.839
campaign this week aimed at

00:00:15.106 --> 00:00:16.841
targeting Russians disaffected

00:00:17.108 --> 00:00:19.010
by the war in Ukraine.

00:00:19.810 --> 00:00:21.212
And basically, life in Russia.

00:00:21.846 --> 00:00:23.047
The video which you see right

00:00:23.314 --> 00:00:24.849
here was first posted on

00:00:25.116 --> 00:00:25.616
telegram.

00:00:25.850 --> 00:00:27.952
A popular unfiltered site

00:00:28.352 --> 00:00:28.653
source --

00:00:28.653 --> 00:00:29.987
source of news in Russia.

00:00:30.354 --> 00:00:32.356
And it includes instructions on

00:00:32.623 --> 00:00:34.825
how to get in touch with the

00:00:35.092 --> 00:00:36.360
CIA anonymously and securely.

00:00:36.360 --> 00:00:37.862
It promises to protect any

00:00:38.362 --> 00:00:39.997
Russian spies who come forward.

00:00:40.364 --> 00:00:41.899
Joining us now is former CIA

00:00:42.366 --> 00:00:44.935
officer, Ronald marks, Ronald

00:00:45.202 --> 00:00:45.936
thank you for joining us.

00:00:46.837 --> 00:00:50.908
Look, I saw clips of this

00:00:51.175 --> 00:00:51.675
video.

00:00:51.842 --> 00:00:53.844
It's quite melancholic, it's

00:00:54.378 --> 00:00:54.878
emotional, it's two minutes,

00:00:55.112 --> 00:00:55.880
long there's no mention of

00:00:56.380 --> 00:00:57.014
Ukraine or Putin.

00:00:57.815 --> 00:00:58.883
And there are cultural

00:00:59.150 --> 00:00:59.617
references.

00:00:59.617 --> 00:01:03.888
Some lines from tolstoy and

00:01:04.388 --> 00:01:05.089
dostoyevsky are quoted there.

00:01:05.923 --> 00:01:07.958
Who do you think the CIA is

00:01:08.392 --> 00:01:09.927
trying to appeal to when it

00:01:10.394 --> 00:01:12.963
comes to recruitment and who

00:01:13.230 --> 00:01:14.398
are they trying to motivate to

00:01:14.398 --> 00:01:14.932
reach out to them?

00:01:15.833 --> 00:01:18.002
&gt;&gt; It's a real in your face

00:01:18.402 --> 00:01:18.836
move.

00:01:18.836 --> 00:01:19.270
No doubt.

00:01:19.270 --> 00:01:22.406
We've had virtual walk-ins for

00:01:22.406 --> 00:01:24.075
years were people sent an email

00:01:24.408 --> 00:01:25.976
saying look, I want to

00:01:26.410 --> 00:01:27.177
volunteer.
This is advertising.

00:01:27.278 --> 00:01:28.846
And it's an indication that we

00:01:29.113 --> 00:01:31.015
really think that they are

00:01:31.282 --> 00:01:31.982
pretty weak.

00:01:32.416 --> 00:01:33.017
Now there is a real problem

00:01:33.284 --> 00:01:33.784
here.

00:01:33.951 --> 00:01:35.853
You've got a younger population

00:01:36.420 --> 00:01:38.022
at this point that is affected

00:01:38.422 --> 00:01:39.056
by what is going on.

00:01:39.890 --> 00:01:40.891
They pick that up a lot

00:01:41.158 --> 00:01:41.658
unclear.

00:01:41.826 --> 00:01:43.060
It's also a way that, if you're

00:01:43.327 --> 00:01:44.428
in the spy game, it's what we

00:01:44.495 --> 00:01:46.030
call it cold pitch.

00:01:47.865 --> 00:01:48.866
You are getting right in there,

00:01:49.133 --> 00:01:49.900
you're saying hey, we'd like to

00:01:50.434 --> 00:01:50.968
have you.

00:01:50.968 --> 00:01:52.970
And if you're the opposition of

00:01:53.237 --> 00:01:54.872
this point you are saying well,

00:01:55.139 --> 00:01:55.906
wait a minute, we've got

00:01:56.440 --> 00:01:56.974
ourselves the problem here.

00:01:57.842 --> 00:02:00.077
So it accomplishes two things

00:02:00.444 --> 00:02:00.945
in the spy game.

00:02:01.212 --> 00:02:02.446
Number, one potential to get

00:02:02.480 --> 00:02:03.914
people who are disaffected in

00:02:04.448 --> 00:02:05.883
who love their country, but are

00:02:06.450 --> 00:02:08.886
not happy with what they see

00:02:09.153 --> 00:02:09.653
going on right now.

00:02:11.822 --> 00:02:12.990
The idea that you're betraying

00:02:13.257 --> 00:02:13.991
your country.

00:02:14.458 --> 00:02:15.092
You're trying to help your

00:02:15.359 --> 00:02:15.859
country.

00:02:15.893 --> 00:02:20.097
But fooling with the opposition,

00:02:20.464 --> 00:02:21.132
letting them know well, you

00:02:21.398 --> 00:02:22.967
guys are vulnerable and that

00:02:23.234 --> 00:02:24.068
means that they've got to spend

00:02:24.468 --> 00:02:26.036
some more resources keeping an

00:02:26.470 --> 00:02:26.937
eye on things.

00:02:26.937 --> 00:02:28.472
&gt;&gt; How effective do you think

00:02:28.506 --> 00:02:29.006
this will be?

00:02:29.206 --> 00:02:30.841
You say this isn't in your face

00:02:31.108 --> 00:02:31.608
move.

00:02:31.809 --> 00:02:34.044
There's a lot of disaffected

00:02:34.478 --> 00:02:35.880
rushes with this Ukraine war.

00:02:37.982 --> 00:02:39.116
This will take a lot of guts

00:02:39.383 --> 00:02:40.151
for someone to actually crossed

00:02:40.484 --> 00:02:40.984
that line.

00:02:41.018 --> 00:02:43.053
Especially regular citizen or

00:02:43.320 --> 00:02:44.155
someone who might be low level

00:02:44.488 --> 00:02:46.023
in the government.

00:02:46.490 --> 00:02:47.458
Because the consequences could

00:02:47.725 --> 00:02:48.225
be quite severe.

00:02:48.692 --> 00:02:53.164
&gt;&gt; Yes, you are dealing with an

00:02:53.430 --> 00:02:54.498
interesting conundrum.

00:02:56.500 --> 00:02:58.169
Nine out of ten people in

00:02:58.502 --> 00:03:00.137
Russia are connected to the

00:03:00.504 --> 00:03:00.838
internet.

00:03:00.838 --> 00:03:02.173
There is a big organization

00:03:02.506 --> 00:03:03.140
inside the Russian government

00:03:03.407 --> 00:03:03.907
that is monitoring it.

00:03:04.141 --> 00:03:04.742
But I can tell you my

00:03:05.009 --> 00:03:05.509
experience, you can't monitor

00:03:05.776 --> 00:03:06.276
everything.

00:03:07.978 --> 00:03:09.280
The idea of appealing to

00:03:09.547 --> 00:03:11.182
someone, it is taking a chance.

00:03:11.982 --> 00:03:15.019
And I would only say, it only

00:03:15.286 --> 00:03:15.786
takes one.

00:03:15.986 --> 00:03:16.520
It only takes two or three.

00:03:16.987 --> 00:03:19.023
You see the kind of damage that

00:03:19.290 --> 00:03:22.126
came out of our army national

00:03:22.526 --> 00:03:23.294
Guard guy up in cape cod.

00:03:23.961 --> 00:03:26.030
Imagine that, now, from the

00:03:26.530 --> 00:03:28.098
Russian standpoint, anybody who

00:03:28.532 --> 00:03:30.134
has access to military, anybody

00:03:30.534 --> 00:03:34.038
who has access to the political

00:03:34.538 --> 00:03:36.040
and can get inside peoples

00:03:36.540 --> 00:03:37.107
strategic or tactical plans.

00:03:37.374 --> 00:03:38.075
Or can inside the head of the

00:03:38.542 --> 00:03:39.542
leadership.

00:03:40.544 --> 00:03:41.345
It doesn't take many.

00:03:42.146 --> 00:03:44.181
A couple, three out of tens of

00:03:44.548 --> 00:03:45.182
thousands, I'm sure they will

00:03:45.449 --> 00:03:46.550
have all kinds of dangles out

00:03:46.717 --> 00:03:49.220
there that will have effort on

00:03:49.486 --> 00:03:51.288
the Russian Intel part to enter

00:03:51.555 --> 00:03:52.556
into the process and enter into

00:03:52.690 --> 00:03:53.190
the game.

00:03:54.992 --> 00:03:56.193
They will tangle people out

00:03:56.560 --> 00:03:58.062
there and pretend they have

00:03:58.562 --> 00:03:59.430
information.
We will have to watch, it we've

00:04:00.064 --> 00:04:00.998
got good people doing

00:04:01.265 --> 00:04:03.000
counter-intelligence but again,

00:04:03.267 --> 00:04:05.135
it is broadcasting in the sense

00:04:05.402 --> 00:04:07.071
of, you are sending an out to 1

00:04:07.338 --> 00:04:07.838
million people.

00:04:08.239 --> 00:04:11.175
Our one 100th of 1% angry

00:04:11.442 --> 00:04:11.942
enough?

00:04:12.009 --> 00:04:12.509
Maybe.

00:04:12.576 --> 00:04:13.076
And if they're in the right

00:04:13.310 --> 00:04:14.211
positions, they can do an

00:04:14.578 --> 00:04:15.112
enormous amount of damage.

00:04:15.379 --> 00:04:16.247
&gt;&gt; Would you say this is the

00:04:16.580 --> 00:04:19.016
right moment for the CIA to

00:04:19.283 --> 00:04:20.117
reach out in this very bold way?

00:04:21.151 --> 00:04:23.153
&gt;&gt; I would say so.

00:04:24.722 --> 00:04:25.222
I like the idea.

00:04:28.859 --> 00:04:32.029
You have what is probably the

00:04:32.596 --> 00:04:33.096
worst engagement from the

00:04:33.230 --> 00:04:35.966
military since Afghanistan from

00:04:36.233 --> 00:04:36.967
the Russians back in the late

00:04:37.234 --> 00:04:38.002
80s, early 90s.

00:04:38.269 --> 00:04:39.069
People are unhappy.

00:04:39.837 --> 00:04:40.337
We know that.

00:04:40.905 --> 00:04:42.840
That house gotten out loud and

00:04:43.107 --> 00:04:43.474
clear.

00:04:43.474 --> 00:04:44.842
You even see some conflict

00:04:45.109 --> 00:04:47.044
internally to Russia.

00:04:47.945 --> 00:04:49.213
What you see on television --

00:04:50.915 --> 00:04:51.982
some of it is pretty baked.

00:04:52.850 --> 00:04:54.018
Young people are unhappy.

00:04:54.285 --> 00:04:55.920
They are being called up in

00:04:56.186 --> 00:04:56.686
this.

00:04:56.921 --> 00:04:58.155
And they are turning, slowly

00:04:58.622 --> 00:05:01.325
but surely, and two of Putin's

00:05:01.992 --> 00:05:02.293
--

00:05:02.293 --> 00:05:03.093
this may be a great moment, in,

00:05:03.360 --> 00:05:04.228
fact to get in there and take

00:05:04.628 --> 00:05:05.195
advantage of people who have

00:05:05.462 --> 00:05:07.097
had enough and would like to

00:05:07.364 --> 00:05:09.099
see this thing over with.

00:05:09.366 --> 00:05:10.868
&gt;&gt; Yeah, it would be

00:05:11.135 --> 00:05:11.936
interesting to see how

